   "title": "Test circuit for response time",
   "page": 5,
   "fixture": true,
   "description": "How tr and tf are measured. A pulse at the input lights the LED, whose cathode is grounded; a reflector plate above the part returns the light to the phototransistor. The transistor's emitter is grounded and its collector is pulled up to VCC through the load RL; the collector node is the test terminal. The output falls while the LED is lit.",
   "parts": [
