 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Sensing",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The LED and the phototransistor face the same way. Light from the LED that bounces off an object in front of the part reaches the phototransistor and raises its collector current; with nothing in front of it the current is the leak current ILEAK. Output peaks with the reflector about 3 mm from the part (Fig.8) and falls on either side, so the working distance is chosen from that curve."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Optical axis",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Detector and emitter centres sit 0.8 mm either side of the optical centre along the 4 mm side, the detector by pins 1 and 2 and the emitter by pins 3 and 4. The optical centre is 1.5 mm from the long edge, in the middle of the 3 mm side."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Stray light",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Ambient light falling on the detecting face can cause false output, and so can LED light reflected into the detector by parts mounted close to it. The black resin blocks visible light."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board layout",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "No copper tracks run on the board under the part, between its terminals, to avoid shorts to its underside. Solder that wicks between the board and the body lowers reliability, so the solder volume is set beforehand to keep it out of that gap."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The opaque resin can crack under force during mounting; placement conditions on automatic machines are checked beforehand."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ageing",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The infrared LED's output falls with use; the design allowance is 50 % over 5 years of operation. The part is not designed to withstand radiation, and its LED is non-coherent."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Reflow once, within the profile in the reflow table. No external force goes on the terminals. How well the joints hold up varies with the line's heating and cool-down, so the method is proven on the real process."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Substances",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "RoHS (2002/95/EC) compliant: the part holds none of Pb, Hg, Cd, Cr(VI), PBB or PBDE. No ozone-depleting chemicals (CFCs, halons, carbon tetrachloride, 1,1,1-trichloroethane) are in the part or used in making it, and no PBBO or PBB flame retardants. All six substances of the Chinese SJ/T 11363-2006 standard are below its limits."
  }
 ],
